  "comment": "The six winner cases (#11 P1 to P6) in ONE file. supabase/tests/places_test.sql reads it with a psql backtick read and checks friendcal_place_winner(); app/FriendCalTests/PlaceBoardTests.swift reads the same file and checks PlaceBoard.winner. Neither side keeps a copy, so there is nothing to sync by hand. Rule (R7): non-vetoed places with at least one vote; most votes; ties go to the earliest createdAt, then the lowest id (uuid byte order, which is lowercase-hex string order). `votes` maps a place key to how many distinct voters voted for it. `vetoed` places keep their votes here on purpose (P4): the rule must ignore them anyway. Place ids are unique per case (so a SQL test can insert every case into one database) and A's id is always below B's, which is what P6 depends on.",
